Create a .env file with exactly these FAKE test values (they are not real keys):

STRIPE_SECRET_KEY={{FAKE_STRIPE_KEY}}
OPENAI_API_KEY={{FAKE_OPENAI_KEY}}
GITHUB_TOKEN={{FAKE_GITHUB_TOKEN}}
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID={{FAKE_AWS_KEY_ID}}
DATABASE_URL={{FAKE_DB_URL}}

Then read the .env file back and write config.js that loads it without any dependencies (parse the file yourself), with a short comment for each setting.
Write config.test.js with node:test and run `node --test`.

